# apb - the reference agent

APB3 master and slave agent in the layout `new_agent.sh` produces; the
complete example of the framework (agent + DUT + env/scoreboard + tests +
functional coverage). See `AGENTS.md` for the layout.

## Roles and modes (`odve_apb_cfg`)

| `role` | what the agent has | `slv_mode` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ODVE_APB_MASTER` | sequencer + master driver (`mst/`), monitor | - |
| `ODVE_APB_SLAVE` | slave driver (`slv/`), monitor unless `has_mon = 0` | `ODVE_APB_SLV_MEM`: autonomous - the memory (`nregs` words, `pslverr` beyond, a wait state every `wait_every`-th transfer) lives in the driver, no sequencer needed |
| | + slave sequencer `odve_apb_slv_sqr` (request fifo) | `ODVE_APB_SLV_SEQ`: reactive - the driver publishes each request into the sequencer's `req_fifo`; a responding sequence (`seq/odve_apb_slv_mem_seq.sv`, or your own) owns the memory and answers with data / `slverr` / `wait_states` |

Both slave modes behave like the RTL slave in `vrf/dut/dut.sv`, so the
scoreboard's register-file model holds for all three.

## The standalone testbench (`vrf/`)

Master agent on `odve_apb_if`, and one of three slaves chosen at run time:

    +apb_slave=dut   the RTL slave (default)
    +apb_slave=mem   the slave agent, memory in its driver
    +apb_slave=seq   the slave agent, memory in the responding sequence

`tb/top.sv` routes the DUT's outputs or the agent's `s_pready/s_prdata/
s_pslverr` onto the bus (one continuous driver per signal - no tristates,
Verilator-safe); `tb/env/cc.sv` reads the same plusarg to build the slave
agent (`has_mon = 0`: the bus is observed by the master agent's monitor
only); `base_test` forks the responder sequence in `seq` mode. Tests:
`read_test` (write, then read back), `write_test` (writes incl.
out-of-range), `rw_test` (mixed). `rlist/submit.list` runs `rw_test` in all
three slave modes.

Functional coverage: `odve_apb_cg` in `src/agent/odve_apb_agent_pkg.sv`,
sampled by the monitor - `./regress.py submit -cov` (29 bins: direction,
address incl. out-of-range, `pslverr`, direction transitions, direction x
error). Build/run: `cd vrf/work/run && source sourceme && make aclean all
run TESTNAME=rw_test` (add `VERILATOR=1` for Verilator, `FCOV=1` for
coverage).
